+++ b/REVIEW.md
@@ -0,0 +1,508 @@
+# Independent adversarial audit: 72-will-it-fly
+
+## Audit result
+
+The candidate contains a legitimate, result-constraining partial-correctness
+proof of the submitted generated program over finite integer lists and integer
+weight bounds. I rebuilt all definitions from source, independently ran every
+positive claim, checked the generated semantics rule by rule, demonstrated
+program-body sensitivity, and obtained the expected failure from a fresh false
+result mutation.
+
+## 1. Input and provenance integrity
+
+### Mode boundary
+
+The rendered mode is `GENERATED_SEMANTICS`. `/reference/reference-semantics`
+does not exist and is not a symlink, which is the required mount state. I did
+not search for or use a hidden reference semantics. There is no infrastructure
+breach.
+
+### Required artifacts and untrusted generation evidence
+
+The following are regular, non-symlink files: `run-input.json`,
+`metrics.json`, `codex-last.txt`, `codex-output.log`, `prompt.py`, `py2mpy.py`,
+`solution.py`, `solution.mpy`, `semantic.k`, `verification.k`, `spec.k`,
+`spec.json`, and `prove.sh`. The structured trace is also a regular file:
+`/candidate/codex-trace/2026/07/22/rollout-2026-07-22T05-34-24-019f8964-1165-7741-99da-1865021e24ee.jsonl`.
+No required source artifact is missing, mistyped, or symlinked.
+
+The untrusted metadata says this was problem `72-will-it-fly`, bare condition,
+with no supplied semantics. `metrics.json` claims generation exit 0 without a
+timeout. `codex-last.txt`, `codex-output.log`, and the trace claim that the
+candidate obtained `#Top`. Those claims were not used as proof evidence.
+
+The candidate also contains ancillary or generated extras: `run-balanced.mpy`,
+`run-unbalanced.mpy`, `spec.json`, `__pycache__/`, and two
+`verification-kompiled*` trees. I ignored all candidate-provided compiled
+definitions, caches, parsed output, and test claims. There are no additional
+candidate helper K source files.
+
+### Trusted comparisons
+
+The candidate prompt is byte-identical to `/reference/prompt.py` (both SHA-256
+`e205ce97af61161bdf9ddb7edca74e7b009f29a138aced873937f6d8a5d23ea6`).
+The candidate translator is byte-identical to `/reference/py2mpy.py` (both
+SHA-256
+`406485eac118431c08ef59f30f79dfa6aa9d5825408917fc5ce7c806e664db16`).
+The detailed type, inventory, hash, log, and trace checks are in
+[`evidence/stage1-integrity.log`](evidence/stage1-integrity.log), generated by
+[`evidence/stage1_integrity.sh`](evidence/stage1_integrity.sh).
+
+Stage 1 result: **pass**.
+
+## 2. Program fidelity and candidate-versus-canonical checks
+
+### Natural-language and canonical contract
+
+For an integer list `q` and integer maximum weight `w`,
+`will_it_fly(q, w)` must return true exactly when:
+
+1. `q` is palindromic; and
+2. `sum(q) <= w`.
+
+The trusted canonical implementation first rejects `sum(q) > w`, then compares
+elements from the two ends until the indices cross. The candidate implementation
+is:
+
+```python
+def will_it_fly(q, w):
+    return q == q[::-1] and sum(q) <= w
+```
+
+On the intended domain this is the same predicate. It has the required entry
+point and no hidden state or helper binding.
+
+### Translation fidelity
+
+In `/tmp/audit-work/72-will-it-fly`, I ran the trusted copied translator:
+
+```text
+python3 trusted-py2mpy.py solution.py > regenerated-solution.mpy
+cmp -s solution.mpy regenerated-solution.mpy
+```
+
+Both commands exited 0. Thus the submitted `solution.mpy` is byte-identical to
+a fresh translation of `solution.py`. Exact command records are
+[`evidence/stage2-regenerate-mpy.log`](evidence/stage2-regenerate-mpy.log) and
+[`evidence/stage2-mpy-byte-identity.log`](evidence/stage2-mpy-byte-identity.log).
+Hashes show the copied trusted translator and canonical implementation remained
+identical to their `/reference` sources in
+[`evidence/stage2-trusted-copy-hashes.log`](evidence/stage2-trusted-copy-hashes.log).
+
+### Independent differential test
+
+[`evidence/differential_test.py`](evidence/differential_test.py) independently
+imports the trusted canonical entry point and generated entry point. It covers:
+
+- all four documented examples;
+- explicit empty, singleton, palindrome/non-palindrome, exact-weight,
+  overweight, negative-value, negative-weight, and large-integer cases;
+- all lists of lengths 0 through 5 over `{-2,-1,0,1,2}` with all weights
+  `-8` through `8`; and
+- 2,500 deterministic generated cases with lengths 0 through 10.
+
+It checked 68,921 input pairs and found zero mismatches. The script itself
+preserves the exact deterministic input generator; the command, exit 0, scope,
+and result are in
+[`evidence/stage2-differential.log`](evidence/stage2-differential.log).
